The core utilities on Radix, which has Linux's system interface through
mlibc: uucore's signal list, realtime signals and broken-pipe check are
Linux's; file systems are described with statvfs, as on Redox, since
mlibc has no statfs, and listed from /processes/mounts (Linux's
/proc/mounts), which Radix writes as mtab lines; and setgroups and the
audit-less id are Linux's.

